<p dir="auto" data-start="2384" data-end="2480">И здесь удобно не пытаться искусственно факторизовать, а сразу решить относительно <span data-start="2467" data-end="2479" role="math" aria-label="\omega_1" data-math-source="\omega_1" data-client-katex-layout=""><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.03588em;">ω</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.3011em;"><span style="top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height:0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>:</p>
<span data-start="2482" data-end="2581" role="math" aria-label="\boxed{
\omega_1
=
\frac{
x(t_1+1)-\frac32t_1^2-2t_1-\frac12
}{
4(t_1+1)(x-t_1)
}.
}
